#!/usr/bin/env node
/*
 * DK STORE: server, database and the finished React website in ONE file.
 * Customer accounts, admin dashboard, stock, revenue, PDF receipts and order emails.
 * No npm install needed to RUN it. Requires Node.js 22.13 or newer.
 *
 * HOW TO RUN (VS Code)
 *   1. Open this file's folder in VS Code (File > Open Folder).
 *   2. Optional: create a file called .env next to this file with lines like:
 *        PORT=3000
 *        ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
 *        ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-a-strong-password
 *        WHATSAPP=923141993887
 *        COOKIE_SECURE=1        (only when the site runs on https)
 *      If ADMIN_PASSWORD is empty, a random one is printed once in the terminal.
 *   3. In the terminal run:   node dk-store.js
 *   4. Store: http://localhost:3000     Admin: http://localhost:3000/admin.html
 *
 * ORDER EMAILS TO dkstore125@gmail.com (optional)
 *   Every new website order can be emailed to the shop. In the Gmail account turn on
 *   2-Step Verification, then create an App Password (Google Account > Security > App passwords).
 *   Add these lines to .env:
 *        SMTP_USER=dkstore125@gmail.com
 *        SMTP_PASS=the 16 letter app password
 *        SHOP_EMAIL=dkstore125@gmail.com
 *        SITE_URL=https://your-website-address   (optional, adds an admin link to the email)
 *   Use the app password, not the normal Gmail password. Without these lines no email is sent.
 *
 * ADMIN SECURITY (all on by default except where noted)
 *   Strong password enforced, lockout after 5 wrong tries, security log, "log out on all devices".
 *   Turn on two-step login (authenticator app) in the admin page > Security. Strongly recommended.
 *   On a real website also set in .env:  COOKIE_SECURE=1  and, behind a host's proxy,  TRUST_PROXY=1
 *   Optional:  ADMIN_IPS=1.2.3.4   (admin only works from these addresses)
 *
 * FORGOT YOUR PASSWORD?
 *   Login screen > "Forgot password?". The reset link is emailed (if SMTP_* is set in .env) or printed in this terminal.
 *   Locked out? Run in this folder:   node dk-store.js --reset-password you@email.com NewPassword123
 *                                     node dk-store.js --disable-2fa you@email.com
 *   After logging in: admin page > Account (change email, name, phone) and Security (password, 2-step login).
 *
 * YOUR WEBSITE ADDRESS
 *   Set SITE_URL=https://yourdomain.pk in .env so search engines and share previews use your real address.
 *   Pages: /privacy /terms /delivery (policy pages, please read and adjust them), a 404 page, robots.txt, sitemap.xml.
 *
 * EDITING THE REACT SITE
 *   The readable React source is in the dk-store-react project (src/ folder).
 *   After changing it run  npm run build  and this server automatically serves the new ./dist
 *   folder instead of the embedded copy. Delete ./dist to go back to the embedded copy.
 *
 * The database is created next to this file in a folder called data (set DATA_DIR to move it).
 * Back up data/store.db regularly. Add to cart works straight away. To count stock, tick Track stock on a product in the admin.
 *
 * FILE MAP (search for these headings)
 *   0. TWO-STEP CODES   1. DATABASE   2. LOGIN AND SECURITY   3. SHOP LOGIC   4. ORDER EMAILS   5. PDF RECEIPTS
 *   6. SERVER AND API ROUTES   7. EMBEDDED REACT BUILD AND IMAGES
 */
